# Java Modular Structure

## Package Layout

Prefer small, focused packages. Create new packages and classes to split logic.

```
com.flinters.aggregator/
├── AggregatorApp.java          # CLI entrypoint only
├── reader/                     # CSV reading
│   └── CsvStreamReader.java
├── model/                      # Domain entities
│   └── CampaignAggregate.java
├── aggregator/                 # Aggregation logic
│   └── CampaignAggregator.java
├── calculator/                 # CTR/CPA computation
│   └── MetricsCalculator.java
├── writer/                     # CSV output
│   └── CsvWriter.java
└── cli/                        # Argument parsing
    └── CliParser.java
```

## When to Extract

- Method > ~25 lines → extract sub-methods or new class
- Class has multiple unrelated responsibilities → split
- Repeated logic in 2+ places → extract to shared util/class
- Complex condition → extract to named method

## Class Size

- Prefer small classes (< 300 lines)
- One public type per file
- Cohesive: all methods relate to one concept

## Dependency Direction

- High-level (CLI, App) depends on low-level (reader, writer)
- Domain/model has no dependencies on I/O
- Use interfaces for testability when needed

## Creating New Files

- Create package directory: `src/main/java/com/flinters/aggregator/<subpackage>/`
- Mirror in test: `src/test/java/com/flinters/aggregator/<subpackage>/`
- One public class per file, same name as file
